{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "d828744f-6c2a-4469-ba4e-b34cc259319c",
    "name": "Quipu Synapse",
    "description": "Complete REST API collection for Quipu Synapse (default port 8001 on the seed node; 8081-8090 for workers) — the distributed, multi-tenant graph database processing engine (Spring Boot + Pekko cluster sharding + YugabyteDB event journal + Kafka ingestion).\n\nCollection variables:\n- {{baseUrl}}    — default http://localhost:8001\n- {{token}}      — bearer JWT sent as Authorization header (RSA-signed, validated for signature/expiry/tenant membership)\n- {{tenantId}}   — tenant identifier (X-Tenant-ID header; fallback when tenantId isn't in the JWT claims)\n- {{namespace}}  — target namespace/schema, default \"public\"\n- {{userId}}     — target user id for User Policy endpoints\n- {{watcherId}}  — a registered watcher id (fill in after Register Watcher)\n- {{queryId}}    — an async/streaming query id (fill in after Async Submit)\n\nAuth notes:\n- Public (no auth): GET /health, GET /actuator/**, GET /namespaces, GET /namespaces/{name}/status, GET /namespaces/{name}/stats.\n- Admin role required: namespace create/enable/disable/delete/historic-ingest-complete/projection-*, User Policy endpoints. Admin role name defaults to ADMIN (configurable via ADMIN_ROLE) and bypasses all per-namespace access policies.\n- All error responses share the shape { \"error\": \"ERROR_CODE\", \"message\": \"...\" } — PLANNING_ERROR/INVALID_REQUEST (400), TIMEOUT (408), EXECUTION_ERROR (500).\n\nThis collection covers every controller EXCEPT the v2 Cypher query-language surface (/api/v2/cypher/**, Cypher2Controller), which already has an exhaustive dedicated collection at postman/cypher2.postman_collection.json (one request per openCypher construct, generated by postman/gen_collection.py). Folder '03 — Query (v2 Cypher Engine)' below covers only the 6 operational endpoints of that engine (query/explain/stream/async submit/poll/cancel) with a minimal example — import cypher2.postman_collection.json separately for full language coverage. Folder '02 — Query (Legacy v1)' covers the older /query/cypher* engine (QueryController), which is a separate implementation from the v2 engine.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "56383100",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/56383100-d828744f-6c2a-4469-ba4e-b34cc259319c?source=collection_link"
  },
